hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"964","Narrated by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala’, narrated by Sufyan, who said: I heard al-Zuhri, beginning and back. If I had sworn against him a hundred times, I would have heard him from Salem. On the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when his journey was serious, he would combine the Maghrib and Isha’ prayers.”"
"965","Yaqoub Al-Dawraqi, Saeed bin Abdul Rahman, and Yahya bin Hakim told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when his journey was serious, he combined the Maghrib and Isha prayers.” And Yahya bin Hakim said: It was Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace"
